response:
 Since  $Z = 13m + 6 = 14n + 5$, $Z - 1$ must be divisible by both 13 and 14, so $Z-1$ is a multiple of $13 \cdot 14= 181$. Therefore the smallest $Z$ must be of the form $181k+1$, for some $k$. Next we need to check for which $k$, $Z>k\cdot14+100$. This gives us
\begin{align*}
k-100 < & 177k-180\\
\Rightarrow 167k < 79\Rightarrow k < \frac{79}{167}
\end{align*}
Thus, $k=1$, so the smallest $Z$ must be $182$. </think> <answer> $182$ </answer>

